From 6676fccb47495c352bf1755c14421058135c5ef5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:48:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AUTO_MEMORIES_MACRO_PLACE: register files not listed are
 inlined
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AUTO_MEMORIES_REGFILES built every register file as a macro: blackboxed
in synthesis, placed by the macro placer and, in `mode netlist`,
dissolved into its cells after macro placement. On a small design the
macro's outline and channels cost more core than the array saves:
riscv32i's register file as a macro does not fit riscv32i's own 62 %
utilisation beside its four FakeRAMs (MPL-0003).

AUTO_MEMORIES_MACRO_PLACE lists the register files to place as macros.
Any other is inlined: gen_memories.py writes only its generated netlist
(no abstract, model liberty or taps) and inline.txt, and synthesis reads
the RTL module as a blackbox and the netlist in its place. Its cells are
then placed, sized and buffered with the rest of the design. A name no
spec builds stops the build.

asap7/regfile lists its RegFile, which keeps the dissolve its tests
exercise. asap7/riscv32i-regfile lists nothing, takes riscv32i's own
utilisation, and its spec writes through a clock gate per word
(`write_style clock_gate`, OpenROAD patch 0010): 955 ps at global route
against the flip-flops' 954, on a core 12 % smaller.

Not upstreamed. Retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS that carries it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
